@page "/providers/"
<LibrarianSeoHead Title="Storage providers — Librarian" Description="Compare Librarian Memory, FileSystem, Redis, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, and Cosmos DB providers: persistence, setup, indexes, and query behavior." Path="/providers/" />
<Section Class="shell page-intro"><Span Class="eyebrow">STORAGE PROVIDERS</Span><H1>Choose your<br /><em>storage.</em></H1><Paragraph>Keep a consistent document API.<br />Choose storage based on persistence, sharing, and query needs.</Paragraph></Section>
<Section Class="shell comparison-section"><Div Class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Storage provider comparison"><table><caption>Provider behavior at a glance</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Memory</th><th scope="col">FileSystem</th><th scope="col">Redis</th><th scope="col">PostgreSQL</th><th scope="col">MongoDB</th><th scope="col">Cosmos DB</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Documents live in</th><td>Process memory</td><td>Memory + JSON file</td><td>Redis</td><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>MongoDB</td><td>Cosmos DB</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Persistence</th><td>Temporary</td><td>Periodic save (~5s)</td><td>Write-through¹</td><td>Committed writes</td><td>Committed writes</td><td>Committed writes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shared across instances</th><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Index lifetime</th><td>Until unload</td><td>Rebuilt on reload</td><td>Persisted in Redis</td><td>Persisted in PostgreSQL</td><td>Persisted in MongoDB</td><td>Persisted in Cosmos DB</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Atomic batches</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes, saved immediately</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Within Cosmos execution limits</td></tr></tbody></table></Div><Paragraph Class="table-note">¹ Redis persistence and eviction configuration determine durability. FileSystem uses one database owner per file; call Save() to flush explicitly.</Paragraph></Section>
<Div Class="shell provider-details">
<Section Id="memory"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">01 / IN PROCESS</Span><H2>Memory</H2><Paragraph>For temporary data, tests, and applications that don’t need storage to survive a restart. No external service to configure.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Soenneker.Librarian.Memory" Class="text-link">Package on NuGet ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Memory" /><CodeSample Label="REGISTER" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Memory.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddMemoryLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph Class="table-note">Scoped registrations are also available. A scoped memory database owns its own data.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
<Section Id="filesystem"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">02 / LOCAL JSON</Span><H2>FileSystem</H2><Paragraph>In-memory access with a JSON file behind it. Designed for a single database owner, with periodic saves and immediate persistence for atomic batches.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Await <code>database.Save()</code> for an explicit flush. Dispose the database’s owner asynchronously to complete shutdown persistence.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL & REGISTER" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.FileSystem" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.FileSystem.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddFileSystemLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><CodeSample Label="APPSETTINGS.JSON" Text="@FileConfig" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="redis"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">03 / SHARED STORAGE</Span><H2>Redis</H2><Paragraph>Shared documents and persisted indexes for multiple application instances. Reads fetch current Redis data; writes update documents and indexes together.</Paragraph><Paragraph>No RedisJSON, Redis Search, or Lua required. Use a non-evicting database; cluster deployments require Redis 8 or later.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/REDIS.md" Class="text-link">Redis setup &amp; guarantees ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Redis" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Redis.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddRedisLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><CodeSample Label="APPSETTINGS.JSON" Text="@RedisConfig" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="postgres"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">04 / PERSISTENT SQL</Span><H2>PostgreSQL</H2><Paragraph>Shared persistent documents with SQL-backed filtering, sorting, paging, and aggregates. Writes and conditional batches commit immediately.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Indexes persist across restarts. Requires PostgreSQL 16 or later. Supply connection credentials through your application’s secret configuration.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/POSTGRES.md" Class="text-link">PostgreSQL setup &amp; queries ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Postgres" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Postgres.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddPostgresLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph>Configure <code>Librarian:Postgres:ConnectionString</code> and <code>Librarian:Postgres:Key</code>.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
<Section Id="mongo"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">05 / NATIVE DOCUMENTS</Span><H2>MongoDB</H2><Paragraph>Immediate document writes, persistent scalar indexes, server-side filtering and paging, and atomic conditional batches across Librarian containers.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Requires a MongoDB replica set or sharded cluster with transaction support. Configure <code>Librarian:Mongo:ConnectionString</code>, <code>DatabaseName</code>, and <code>Key</code>. Optional <code>CollectionName</code> defaults to <code>librarian</code>.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Mongo" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Mongo.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddMongoLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="cosmos"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">06 / AZURE DOCUMENTS</Span><H2>Cosmos DB for NoSQL</H2><Paragraph>Uses your existing Soenneker Cosmos utilities to create the database and physical container on first access. Documents use native Cosmos point operations, JSON indexes, and SDK LINQ queries.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Each Librarian database key occupies one logical partition under <code>/partitionKey</code>. Conditional batches use a lazily created Cosmos stored procedure so checks and writes remain atomic. Cosmos request, execution time, and partition limits apply.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Cosmos" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Cosmos.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddCosmosLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph>Uses <code>Azure:Cosmos:Endpoint</code>, <code>AccountKey</code>, <code>DatabaseName</code>, <code>DatabaseThroughput</code>, <code>DatabaseThroughputType</code>, and the application's <code>Environment</code>. Optional <code>Librarian:Cosmos:ContainerName</code> and <code>Key</code> both default to <code>librarian</code>.</Paragraph><Paragraph>The Cosmos utilities enable database and container creation by default. Their <code>EnsureDatabaseOnFirstUse</code> and <code>EnsureContainerOnFirstUse</code> settings remain available for pre-provisioned environments.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
</Div>
<Section Class="shell provider-ending"><H2>Same API. Know the differences.</H2><Paragraph>Memory and FileSystem can fall back to local evaluation for unsupported queries. Redis and PostgreSQL reject unsupported expressions. MongoDB and Cosmos delegate LINQ translation to their native SDKs, including supported grouping, aggregates, and projections. Their native query semantics and translation limits apply; unsupported expressions are rejected without client-side fallback. Review query support before moving a workload between providers.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/QUERY-CAPABILITIES.md" Class="button">Compare query capabilities ↗</Anchor></Section>
@code {
    private const string FileConfig = """
        {
          "Librarian": {
            "FileSystem": { "FilePath": "data/librarian.json" }
          }
        }
        """;
    private const string RedisConfig = """
        {
          "Azure": { "Redis": { "ConnectionString": "localhost:6379" } },
          "Librarian": {
            "Redis": { "Key": "my-app:librarian" }
          }
        }
        """;
}
